      "problem": "If $A={0,x,x}$, then $|A|=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n0,\\,x\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $A$ has $2$ elements, its cardinality is $|A|=\\text{2}.$",
