    "q-181469": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181469",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "If $S={1,{2,3},4,{5,6}}$, then $|S|=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $S$ is the number of elements in $S.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $S:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,{2,3},\\,4,\\,{5,6}\n$$\n\nNote that ${2,3}$ and ${5,6}$ each count as single elements of $S.$\n\nSince $S$ has $4$ elements, the cardinality is $|S|=4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
