      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $T={{},x,y,{v,x,{w}}},$ then $|T|=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $T$ is the number of elements in $T.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $T:$\n\n$$\n{},\\,x,\\,y,\\,{v,x,{w}},\n$$\n\nNote that ${v,x,{w}}$ and ${}$ count as single elements of $T.$\n\nSince $T$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|T|=4.$",
